WEBVTT

00:00.560 --> 00:03.190
Everyone, advance while Tsubasa's still here!

00:03.190 --> 00:04.400
Let's stretch that lead!

00:04.400 --> 00:05.810
Oh, crap!

00:05.810 --> 00:07.150
Everyone! Fall back!

00:07.820 --> 00:09.030
The roles are reversed!

00:09.030 --> 00:11.150
This time, it's Shutetsu's counter-attack!

00:11.150 --> 00:12.900
Like I'd let you pass!

00:13.570 --> 00:14.160
Taki!

00:15.110 --> 00:16.160
Okay!

00:16.160 --> 00:17.530
All right, let's go for the second goal!

00:18.240 --> 00:18.950
What?!

00:19.450 --> 00:22.870
Tsubasa steals the ball back from Taki.

00:25.580 --> 00:26.210
He's going to shoot!

00:26.210 --> 00:27.460
Shoot!

00:27.460 --> 00:28.090
What?

00:28.500 --> 00:30.340
Can this be...

00:30.340 --> 00:34.880
Tsubasa takes an extra long shot from Nankatsu's own side!

00:36.050 --> 00:38.720
Wakabayashi firmly catches the ball!

00:40.720 --> 00:42.060
What a surprise!

00:42.060 --> 00:44.100
Who would have thought that he'd shoot from such a place?

00:44.100 --> 00:46.020
But it didn't become a goal.

00:46.020 --> 00:48.110
Are you panicking, Tsubasa?

00:48.110 --> 00:49.770
You were too focused on shooting.

00:49.770 --> 00:52.320
Football is played with eleven people...

00:52.320 --> 00:54.570
You won't score a goal if you're fighting alone!

01:08.080 --> 01:13.710
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:08.080 --> 01:13.710
<i>koronde toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:13.710 --> 01:19.300
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:13.710 --> 01:19.300
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:19.300 --> 01:24.980
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:19.300 --> 01:24.980
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidou ga</i>

01:24.980 --> 01:32.900
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:24.980 --> 01:32.900
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:32.900 --> 01:38.660
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:32.900 --> 01:38.660
<i>goal o soreta kibou ga atte mo</i>

01:38.660 --> 01:47.160
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:38.660 --> 01:47.160
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:47.160 --> 01:52.960
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:47.160 --> 01:52.960
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:52.960 --> 01:58.880
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:52.960 --> 01:58.880
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

01:58.880 --> 02:00.510
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:00.510 --> 02:07.770
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:00.510 --> 02:07.770
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:07.770 --> 02:10.730
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Go, our kicks!</i>

02:07.770 --> 02:10.730
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kick o</i>

02:10.730 --> 02:15.650
<i>Leap out into a huge TV</i>

02:10.730 --> 02:15.650
<i>tobidasou dodekai TV</i>

02:26.040 --> 02:30.250
<b><b>Episode 8:
THE BIRTH OF NANKATSU'S GOLDEN DUO!</b></b>

02:27.250 --> 02:28.500
He cut through!

02:28.500 --> 02:31.630
Tsubasa has stolen the ball again!

02:31.630 --> 02:34.000
He's the only one Nankatsu can rely on.

02:34.000 --> 02:36.210
Don't bother marking anyone but Tsubasa!

02:40.430 --> 02:41.260
What?

02:41.890 --> 02:43.510
Nice pass!

02:43.510 --> 02:48.520
Wow! Tsubasa lures the defense in before executing a wonderfully precise pass!

02:48.520 --> 02:50.520
Everyone, this is our chance!

02:50.520 --> 02:52.610
Remember our special training with Roberto!

02:52.610 --> 02:53.610
Okay!

02:53.610 --> 02:55.110
Calm down.

02:55.110 --> 02:56.610
Take a good look around you.

02:56.610 --> 02:58.530
All right, inside!

02:59.360 --> 03:00.280
Let's go!

03:00.280 --> 03:00.950
Hey!

03:02.030 --> 03:02.700
Hey!

03:02.700 --> 03:04.030
Once more... go!

03:04.030 --> 03:05.790
These guys...

03:05.790 --> 03:07.330
Even though they're just Nankatsu...

03:08.330 --> 03:10.370
Nankatsu's passes are connecting for the first time!

03:10.370 --> 03:14.000
Shutetsu, lured in by Tsubasa, can't react in time!

03:14.000 --> 03:15.710
That Tsubasa...

03:15.710 --> 03:18.630
Was this what he was aiming for, drawing all that attention with that shot?

03:18.630 --> 03:20.010
If that's really the case,

03:20.010 --> 03:21.880
his sense of the game is excellent!

03:21.880 --> 03:22.720
Take this!

03:22.720 --> 03:23.840
All right!

03:23.840 --> 03:26.560
Tsubasa's long pass barely stayed in bounds!

03:26.560 --> 03:27.470
Stop him!

03:27.470 --> 03:28.270
Damn it!

03:28.270 --> 03:31.020
Nankatsu's got a great rhythm right now.

03:31.020 --> 03:32.440
Go!

03:32.440 --> 03:33.730
Ishizaki crosses the ball!

03:33.730 --> 03:36.400
That's a nice cross!

03:39.530 --> 03:42.070
Wakabayashi's off-balance from the decoy!

03:42.070 --> 03:44.530
Tsubasa runs in for the ball!

03:45.120 --> 03:47.160
A diving header!

03:47.160 --> 03:50.290
Is it the game-tying goal for Nankatsu?

03:52.040 --> 03:53.670
Oh, the ball bounces erratically!

03:53.670 --> 03:56.290
Nankatsu can't score the game-tying goal!

03:56.290 --> 03:59.050
Tsubasa! That was close!

03:59.050 --> 04:01.630
That's the spirit! Keep going like that!

04:01.630 --> 04:02.970
What a pity...

04:02.970 --> 04:04.970
That was close!

04:04.970 --> 04:06.970
Everyone, we're on a roll!

04:06.970 --> 04:08.760
Let's keep this up!

04:08.760 --> 04:10.220
Okay!

04:14.100 --> 04:16.060
Luck is also a part of talent...

04:16.520 --> 04:20.610
Sorry, Tsubasa, but we'll be winning this match.

04:20.610 --> 04:21.490
All right!

04:21.490 --> 04:22.610
It's time for the "birdcage"!

04:22.610 --> 04:24.450
Eh? The "birdcage"?

04:24.450 --> 04:26.620
Wait... Are we really doing that?

04:26.990 --> 04:28.330
Did he say birdcage?

04:29.620 --> 04:30.910
Birdcage?

04:34.250 --> 04:37.000
Time is ticking away.

04:37.000 --> 04:42.340
Who would have thought about such a turn of events before the match?

04:42.340 --> 04:44.180
How many times has it been now?

04:44.180 --> 04:46.470
Tsubasa is going to steal the ball again!

04:46.470 --> 04:47.430
Here he comes!

04:47.430 --> 04:49.010
Make sure to keep an eye on him!

04:49.010 --> 04:50.470
Pass the ball quickly!

04:50.470 --> 04:51.720
Yeah.

04:52.600 --> 04:54.390
All right. There!

04:55.060 --> 04:55.900
This isn't good...

04:55.900 --> 04:57.440
I can't steal the ball like this!

04:59.940 --> 05:01.900
Here I go, I'm crossing...

05:02.900 --> 05:05.360
Nah, like I'd do that!

05:05.910 --> 05:09.120
Shutetsu is defensively passing the ball around, away from the Nankatsu players!

05:09.120 --> 05:12.620
They have absolutely no intention of attacking.

05:13.080 --> 05:14.790
Birdcage...

05:14.790 --> 05:18.630
I wouldn't have expected an elementary school's team to use such a tactic.

05:19.210 --> 05:21.300
You start by keeping the ball on your side.

05:21.300 --> 05:24.050
Once you lure the opponent in, you pass the ball around center field,

05:24.050 --> 05:26.050
and prevent them from moving around.

05:26.050 --> 05:29.800
This tactic is used by pros to buy some time.

05:31.470 --> 05:35.350
With this, it'll be difficult for you to do anything until the game is over.

05:35.890 --> 05:39.480
Like birds trapped in a cage...

05:41.150 --> 05:42.980
That's cheap, Shutetsu!

05:42.980 --> 05:46.650
Don't you know how to play fair?

05:47.070 --> 05:47.860
They did it again!

05:47.860 --> 05:49.450
They turned the ball around again.

05:49.450 --> 05:54.870
Shutetsu might be the national tournament's reigning champion, but,

05:54.870 --> 05:57.250
is it really okay for them to show such half-hearted play?

05:57.920 --> 05:59.540
Say what you will!

05:59.540 --> 06:01.540
It's precisely because we're the reigning champions,

06:01.540 --> 06:03.250
that we can't afford to lose.

06:03.250 --> 06:05.260
Espcially to you, Tsubasa Ozora.

06:06.920 --> 06:08.300
Wakabayashi...

06:09.140 --> 06:11.510
Tsubasa! I'll get the ball back!

06:12.100 --> 06:13.760
I'll send it to you as soon as I get it,

06:13.760 --> 06:15.390
so get in front of the goal!

06:15.390 --> 06:16.730
We have no choice!

06:16.730 --> 06:17.520
Okay!

06:17.520 --> 06:19.520
We'll be playing against Ishizaki?

06:19.520 --> 06:21.520
Well, I couldn't ask for more.

06:22.770 --> 06:24.280
I'll definitely get it back!

06:30.240 --> 06:32.740
Ishizaki just can't steal the ball!

06:32.740 --> 06:33.620
The score is still 1-0,

06:33.620 --> 06:35.870
and there's very little time left!

06:35.870 --> 06:38.000
Still, if they all press together,

06:38.000 --> 06:39.540
they will leave their defense weakened,

06:39.540 --> 06:42.210
and Shutetsu might score their second goal.

06:42.210 --> 06:45.340
Ishizaki, you are the captain, right?

06:45.340 --> 06:47.210
Hang in there just a little longer!

06:47.210 --> 06:49.840
Yeah! Hang in there, Nankatsu!

06:49.840 --> 06:52.890
You've come this far against Shutetsu!

06:52.890 --> 06:54.600
Just hold out a little bit longer!

06:55.850 --> 06:58.140
What do you mean "you've come this far"?

06:58.140 --> 07:02.190
It wasn't us... it was him!

07:02.190 --> 07:05.110
It's all thanks to Tsubasa that our lame football team

07:05.110 --> 07:07.110
was able to come this far.

07:07.610 --> 07:09.650
Winning against Nishigaoka,

07:09.650 --> 07:13.660
practicing that hard, seriously believing we can beat Shutetsu,

07:14.450 --> 07:17.950
and keeping it to just a one-goal lead in this match,

07:17.950 --> 07:20.960
isn't that all thanks to Tsubasa?

07:21.710 --> 07:22.920
So, at the very least,

07:22.920 --> 07:26.630
I have to take this ball and pass it to Tsubasa.

07:26.630 --> 07:30.260
Otherwise, all of our work will have meant nothing!

07:30.260 --> 07:33.090
Oh, the referee is looking at his watch.

07:33.090 --> 07:35.550
Time is almost up!

07:35.550 --> 07:37.680
Damn it, this can't go on like this.

07:37.680 --> 07:38.520
It's now or never!

07:38.520 --> 07:40.230
I'll go and save our captain.

07:41.020 --> 07:42.400
Me too!

07:42.400 --> 07:43.900
And me!

07:45.230 --> 07:46.320
What?

07:46.320 --> 07:48.190
Let's change sides.

07:48.190 --> 07:49.360
Got it.

07:50.190 --> 07:51.650
Changing sides?!

07:51.650 --> 07:52.740
Then...!

07:52.740 --> 07:53.990
I'm counting on you, Taki!

07:55.120 --> 07:57.790
Ishizaki predicted the course of the pass!

07:57.790 --> 07:58.790
That's dangerous!

08:03.830 --> 08:04.670
My foot...!

08:04.670 --> 08:07.460
That's an intense clash and, ball goes...

08:07.460 --> 08:10.010
We won't get another chance if we can't get the ball here!

08:11.670 --> 08:13.680
Tsubasa!

08:16.390 --> 08:19.100
The pass reaches Tsubasa!

08:19.100 --> 08:20.390
Ishizaki!

08:27.610 --> 08:32.450
Finally, Nankatsu breaks free of the cage!

08:38.620 --> 08:40.750
That's all I can do!

08:40.750 --> 08:41.870
I'm counting on you!

08:42.330 --> 08:45.000
Ishizaki put his body on the line and passed this ball to me.

08:45.000 --> 08:46.790
I won't let it go to waste.

08:47.210 --> 08:48.290
Here I go!

08:48.290 --> 08:49.500
Is he coming?

08:49.920 --> 08:52.760
With this, we'll finally settle our score.

08:52.760 --> 08:53.590
The one who'll win,

08:54.300 --> 08:56.340
is us, Shutetsu!

08:56.340 --> 08:57.510
It's time to score!

08:57.510 --> 08:59.100
If you can't score here,

08:59.100 --> 09:00.770
your father's disowning you!

09:00.770 --> 09:02.850
And so is your mother!

09:03.770 --> 09:06.480
We're deep into stoppage time.

09:06.480 --> 09:09.360
This might be Nankatsu's last chance.

09:10.980 --> 09:12.070
Is he for real?

09:12.070 --> 09:13.570
Tsubasa has set his eyes on the goal

09:13.570 --> 09:14.650
and advances alone.

09:15.070 --> 09:15.910
All right!

09:15.910 --> 09:17.070
I'm almost there!

09:17.070 --> 09:18.620
Not so fast!

09:19.240 --> 09:21.040
We're still here.

09:21.040 --> 09:23.160
We won't let you beat us by yourself.

09:23.160 --> 09:25.160
We're going to crush you!

09:25.160 --> 09:26.170
Take this!

09:27.420 --> 09:31.130
Tsubasa jumps and evades Kisugi's sliding tackle.

09:31.130 --> 09:34.720
However, the giant Takasugi...!

09:34.720 --> 09:35.970
Tsubasa!

09:39.640 --> 09:41.390
No one can catch up to him!

09:42.010 --> 09:44.020
He's one-on-one with the goalkeeper...

09:44.020 --> 09:45.140
Wait, not yet!

09:45.140 --> 09:47.900
There's another one there... Izawa, the midfielder!

09:48.310 --> 09:49.400
I won't let you pass!

09:49.400 --> 09:50.900
Which side will he attack from?

09:52.360 --> 09:53.610
What?

09:53.610 --> 09:57.030
He has finally managed to shake everyone off!

09:57.030 --> 09:58.660
Tsubasa Ozora...

09:58.660 --> 10:00.160
What a guy he is!

10:00.160 --> 10:03.120
No matter what we do, we can't stop him at all!

10:03.120 --> 10:04.330
Tsubasa...

10:04.330 --> 10:06.540
Just come closer.

10:07.210 --> 10:09.830
Oh, Tsubasa immediately prepares to shoot.

10:09.830 --> 10:12.800
Why are you not shooting after entering the penalty area, Tsubasa?

10:12.800 --> 10:14.050
This guy...

10:14.050 --> 10:15.800
He just wants to shoot outside of the penalty area.

10:16.760 --> 10:19.930
Tsubasa's decisive long shot!

10:19.930 --> 10:21.430
The same course, again?

10:22.760 --> 10:23.760
It's useless!

10:23.760 --> 10:27.440
I don't concede goals from outside of the penalty area!

10:27.810 --> 10:29.900
Fine play, Wakabayashi!

10:29.900 --> 10:31.940
However, the ball is still in play!

10:31.940 --> 10:33.340
- Go in!
- Don't go in!

10:33.980 --> 10:36.070
The ball hits the crossbar!

10:36.360 --> 10:37.320
I win!

10:37.320 --> 10:39.820
Nankatsu couldn't tie the game!

10:41.700 --> 10:44.080
Tsubasa...!

10:44.080 --> 10:45.330
He's flying!

10:45.330 --> 10:47.330
Is this...

10:52.080 --> 10:54.340
It's an overhead kick!

11:01.010 --> 11:04.350
It's the game-tying goal!

11:05.720 --> 11:07.310
I did it...

11:07.310 --> 11:10.060
I did it!

11:11.310 --> 11:12.310
All right!

11:13.400 --> 11:15.320
Tsubasa...

11:17.820 --> 11:20.240
This can't be...

11:23.910 --> 11:24.830
Woah!

11:24.830 --> 11:29.830
SIGN: Shutetsu vs. Nankatsu

11:24.830 --> 11:27.500
This marks the end of the match.

11:27.500 --> 11:29.830
Neither team were able to settle the score in 40 minutes.

11:30.250 --> 11:33.330
Therefore, after a 5-minute break,

11:33.330 --> 11:36.590
we'll have two more 5-minute halves of extra time for this match.

11:38.960 --> 11:41.220
Everyone, you did well.

11:41.220 --> 11:43.050
Still, Tsubasa...

11:43.050 --> 11:44.470
I'm surprised!

11:44.470 --> 11:46.470
That trick I showed you the first time we met,

11:46.890 --> 11:48.560
that post-rebound overhead kick.

11:49.230 --> 11:50.430
It could have been a coincidence,

11:50.430 --> 11:52.810
I wouldn't have expected you to use it in an actual match.

11:53.350 --> 11:58.690
But I've been practising for it so when the ball hit the post I was able to jump at the same moment.

11:58.690 --> 12:01.200
That's so cool, Tsubasa!

12:01.200 --> 12:02.990
Overtime, huh...

12:02.990 --> 12:04.620
That's no good.

12:04.620 --> 12:06.240
Oh right, Ishizaki...

12:06.830 --> 12:08.740
Is your foot all right?

12:08.740 --> 12:09.660
What are you talking about?

12:09.660 --> 12:11.120
It wasn't a big deal.

12:11.120 --> 12:13.040
See, I am standing just fine.

12:13.040 --> 12:15.040
Look, I can do thi—

12:19.090 --> 12:20.420
Ishizaki!

12:22.760 --> 12:25.720
Ishizaki, you can't play like this!

12:25.720 --> 12:26.470
Stupid!

12:26.470 --> 12:28.010
Such an injury would never...

12:28.810 --> 12:29.890
It won't do.

12:32.980 --> 12:34.440
Who the hell are you?

12:35.900 --> 12:37.730
I'm Taro Misaki.

12:41.190 --> 12:43.610
Captain...

12:49.910 --> 12:51.290
It's over...

13:03.720 --> 13:05.090
Ow!

13:05.090 --> 13:06.970
As I thought, it's a sprain.

13:06.970 --> 13:09.310
It'll take at least three days to heal.

13:09.310 --> 13:12.270
Why do you know stuff like that!?

13:12.270 --> 13:16.850
I read a lot on the train, since my father travels often for work.

13:16.850 --> 13:21.400
A book I read about football had first-aid techniques inside.

13:21.400 --> 13:22.650
Football?

13:22.650 --> 13:23.570
Yeah.

13:23.570 --> 13:28.780
Well, now what do we do? We only have 11 players.

13:28.780 --> 13:31.450
What? Ishizaki's injured?

13:31.450 --> 13:34.040
Yeah. Can anyone come as a replacement?

13:34.040 --> 13:36.710
Can anybody here play football?

13:36.710 --> 13:38.210
Football?

13:38.210 --> 13:39.460
No way.

13:39.460 --> 13:41.210
Impossible.

13:41.210 --> 13:43.630
If that's the case, then I'll...

13:43.630 --> 13:44.720
Boss!?

13:44.720 --> 13:48.890
If I do that, I can play with Tsubasa after all!

13:48.890 --> 13:49.850
What!

13:49.850 --> 13:54.060
All right, then! I, the great Hanji Urabe, will go!

13:54.060 --> 13:57.730
No. I'll go. Surely, I will be of more use than him.

13:57.730 --> 14:00.650
Wait. This is a match between Nankatsu and Shutetsu,

14:00.650 --> 14:02.150
people from other schools are...

14:02.150 --> 14:03.030
I'll go.

14:03.030 --> 14:04.030
No. I'll go.

14:06.820 --> 14:08.780
Captain! Where are you going?

14:08.780 --> 14:10.160
I told you.

14:10.170 --> 14:15.790
This was a match between me and Tsubasa to find out if he could score against me.

14:16.460 --> 14:19.920
I lost that match.

14:19.920 --> 14:23.340
You guys can handle the extra time.

14:23.340 --> 14:24.800
Captain!

14:24.800 --> 14:26.550
Wait, Wakabayashi.

14:31.470 --> 14:32.720
Ah!

14:37.770 --> 14:39.060
Mr. Mikami!

14:39.060 --> 14:40.770
Stop acting like a spoiled kid, Genzo!

14:40.770 --> 14:44.070
You give up a single goal, so now you're running away?

14:44.070 --> 14:46.030
You should be ashamed of yourself.

14:47.030 --> 14:50.110
This isn't how I've coached you!

14:50.110 --> 14:54.040
From now on, I won't be your coach anymore, Genzo.

14:56.790 --> 15:01.710
Wakabayashi. I'm the one who made you captain.

15:01.710 --> 15:03.750
But, these guys are the ones who have

15:03.750 --> 15:05.960
trusted and supported you this far.

15:06.710 --> 15:10.720
Are you going to turn your back to them now?

15:15.720 --> 15:18.310
It's a showdown! Whoever wins joins the match!

15:18.310 --> 15:19.810
No hard feelings!

15:19.810 --> 15:22.730
Bring it on, don't come crying later!

15:24.230 --> 15:25.860
Those guys...

15:25.860 --> 15:28.690
Say, would it be okay if I go?

15:28.690 --> 15:32.620
What? Don't be stupid, you're not in Nankatsu either.

15:32.620 --> 15:34.660
I'm in Nankatsu too.

15:35.490 --> 15:37.450
I got transferred today.

15:40.460 --> 15:41.120
Ah!

15:42.790 --> 15:43.960
Eh! You're...

15:43.960 --> 15:47.000
I'm going in for the injured. Taro Misaki.

15:47.000 --> 15:48.210
Don't joke around!

15:48.210 --> 15:49.300
The one playing is...

15:49.300 --> 15:50.630
Us!

15:56.180 --> 15:57.310
He's good.

15:57.310 --> 15:59.140
That...

16:02.190 --> 16:03.690
Woah!

16:03.690 --> 16:06.270
It's a little big but bear with it.

16:06.270 --> 16:09.190
Okay. Let's get along, Tsubasa.

16:09.610 --> 16:12.200
Yeah. Same here, Misaki.

16:19.910 --> 16:23.540
I lost to Tsubasa.

16:25.330 --> 16:30.420
But, before that, I'm Shutetsu's captain.

16:33.050 --> 16:35.850
We'll definitely win this!

16:35.850 --> 16:37.810
Captain!

16:38.350 --> 16:39.930
Yeah.

16:40.980 --> 16:43.940
It's time for extra time to begin!

16:43.940 --> 16:48.150
Let's go! Shutetsu's football starts from now!

16:48.150 --> 16:49.190
Yeah!

16:49.190 --> 16:52.900
All right! 10 more minutes! Give your best!

16:52.900 --> 16:54.200
Yeah!

16:54.200 --> 16:57.120
I'm counting on you guys! Do your best in my stead!

17:00.490 --> 17:03.120
That's more like it, Genzo.

17:03.960 --> 17:08.250
The first half starts! Nankatsu kicks off.

17:08.250 --> 17:12.380
What? Now there's yet another guy we don't recognize...

17:12.380 --> 17:13.510
Yeah.

17:14.510 --> 17:18.010
Can you hear it? All this cheering...

17:18.010 --> 17:19.720
Let's win this, together!

17:19.720 --> 17:20.770
Oh...!

17:21.560 --> 17:24.310
Hey,I wonder how the next town be like...

17:25.520 --> 17:29.650
I see. Tsubasa and I are the same...

17:29.650 --> 17:32.610
Tsubasa, I have a request.

17:33.690 --> 17:35.200
As soon as the whistle blows,

17:35.200 --> 17:37.700
give me the ball and run forward.

17:37.700 --> 17:39.950
Move wherever you want after that.

17:39.950 --> 17:41.330
Okay.

17:44.460 --> 17:45.790
I'll take the ball.

17:51.460 --> 17:53.460
Who the hell is this guy?

17:58.890 --> 17:59.970
What...

17:59.970 --> 18:00.970
Is he?

18:04.640 --> 18:07.140
Amazing! Right to my feet!

18:07.140 --> 18:12.320
A through pass! And a gentle touch, keeping his target in mind!

18:12.320 --> 18:13.820
Eh! You...

18:20.030 --> 18:21.830
You're awesome, Misaki.

18:21.830 --> 18:25.790
You know what I'm thinking just by looking at my eyes!

18:25.790 --> 18:28.540
You too, Tsubasa!

18:28.540 --> 18:34.550
That #11 is Taro Misaki. He apparently transferred to Nankatsu today.

18:34.550 --> 18:36.920
They still had a guy like this in their arsenal...

18:36.920 --> 18:38.720
What are you worried about? It's okay.

18:38.720 --> 18:39.550
Huh?

18:39.550 --> 18:43.810
Genzo won't concede a goal when he's like this.

18:43.810 --> 18:47.060
He only saw Tsubasa as his opponent until now.

18:47.060 --> 18:51.560
But, right now, his eyes are those of a captain, aiming to win with his team.

18:51.980 --> 18:56.240
Now, Genzo is keeping track of the movements of both the players

18:56.240 --> 18:59.820
and the ball, as if they were in the palm of his hand.

18:59.820 --> 19:01.660
And since he's no longer distracted,

19:01.660 --> 19:04.290
he can react to anyone's shot.

19:10.120 --> 19:13.590
Taro Misaki, you're good too.

19:14.090 --> 19:18.510
You've grown again thanks to this match, Genzo.

19:18.510 --> 19:20.760
You're the real deal.

19:20.760 --> 19:22.760
We did it, coach!

19:22.760 --> 19:25.010
We're dictating the pace this extra time.

19:25.640 --> 19:26.890
Tsubasa and Misaki...

19:26.890 --> 19:30.770
Nankatsu can't lose as long as we have these two!

19:30.770 --> 19:33.150
If I knew this would happen, Ishizaki,

19:33.150 --> 19:35.900
I would've had you get hurt earlier!

19:35.900 --> 19:37.190
Eh...

19:37.190 --> 19:39.530
That's mean, coach...

19:40.570 --> 19:45.450
That marks the end of the first half in extra time!

19:46.910 --> 19:49.250
Genzo, nice leadership.

19:49.250 --> 19:50.870
Mr. Mikami!

19:50.870 --> 19:52.500
Everybody, hang in there.

19:52.500 --> 19:54.340
Just a little bit longer.

19:54.340 --> 19:57.550
Five more minutes. They're also struggling.

19:57.550 --> 20:00.050
Give it your all!

20:00.050 --> 20:01.260
Yes!

20:01.260 --> 20:04.510
It's too late to turn back now. Five more minutes and that's it.

20:04.890 --> 20:08.140
Everyone, give it your all! Leave no regrets on the field!

20:08.140 --> 20:09.180
Yes!

20:09.560 --> 20:11.940
That's right! Five more minutes!

20:11.940 --> 20:14.190
We'll give it everyting we've got!

20:16.650 --> 20:20.240
All that's left is five more minutes of the second half!

20:20.240 --> 20:24.120
Shutetsu starts the second half with their kick-off!

20:24.120 --> 20:25.780
Run, Taki! Let's go for a blitz!

20:26.490 --> 20:28.540
Shutetsu goes for it right away!

20:28.540 --> 20:32.040
The playmaker Izawa sends off a thunderous long pass!

20:33.170 --> 20:34.040
Wha—

20:34.580 --> 20:38.050
The lead attacker Taki dribbles forward in his characteristic style!

20:38.050 --> 20:41.920
Oh? He sends the ball back to the midfielder Izawa.

20:41.920 --> 20:43.510
Is he going to shoot?

20:44.140 --> 20:46.260
No, he chips it over the defender!

20:46.260 --> 20:50.270
Kisugi gets to it first and goes for a volley!

20:51.350 --> 20:54.400
The deflected ball goes over the crossbar!

20:57.110 --> 20:59.360
It's the first corner kick in this extra time!

20:59.360 --> 21:01.030
It's a chance for Shutetsu!

21:01.030 --> 21:02.780
Everyone, be careful!

21:02.780 --> 21:05.870
Shutetsu's set-play is something you need to be wary of!

21:10.910 --> 21:12.040
Captain!

21:12.040 --> 21:13.410
Here, Taki!

21:13.410 --> 21:17.670
What?! Wakabayashi, the goalkeeper, has come forward to join the attack!

21:18.920 --> 21:22.090
It's a cross to Wakabayashi!

21:24.630 --> 21:25.590
He shoots!

21:25.590 --> 21:29.390
The power is much greater than any field player's!

21:31.140 --> 21:34.100
Nice shot, Wakabayashi!

21:34.770 --> 21:36.100
Yeah!

21:36.100 --> 21:39.110
It's 2-1! Shutetsu leads!

21:39.110 --> 21:43.610
The game's winner might have been decided with this goal!

21:43.610 --> 21:47.070
Captain. If we look at the remaining time, birdcage...

21:47.070 --> 21:49.490
What, do you guys like birdcage?

21:50.370 --> 21:54.710
That's enough. That's a strategy to run away.

21:54.710 --> 21:56.120
Rather than protect this one point,

21:56.120 --> 21:59.630
let's score another and secure our win. What do you say?

21:59.630 --> 22:01.000
Captain!

22:01.000 --> 22:05.340
Amazing! Wakabayashi... really is amazing!

22:05.340 --> 22:09.430
But the match isn't over! It's our turn now!

22:09.430 --> 22:10.510
Yeah!

22:11.180 --> 22:13.310
I won't let them say they lost

22:13.310 --> 22:15.060
because I came in.

22:15.730 --> 22:18.650
All right! Time to counter-attack!

22:38.790 --> 22:44.670
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.670
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.670 --> 22:50.680
<i>suguremono zo to machijuu sawagu</i>

22:44.670 --> 22:50.680
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.680 --> 22:56.680
<i>chouchou samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.680 --> 22:56.680
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.680 --> 23:01.690
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.680 --> 23:01.690
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:02.820 --> 23:08.070
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:02.820 --> 23:08.070
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:14.990
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:14.990
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.290 --> 23:21.040
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.040 --> 23:26.050
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.040 --> 23:26.050
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.260 --> 23:33.220
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.260 --> 23:33.220
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.220 --> 23:39.100
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.100 --> 23:46.070
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.100 --> 23:46.070
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.610 --> 23:58.750
COMING UP, EPISODE 9:
A HAPPY ENDING
